==========================================================================
WHY THIS FILE CHANGED, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER
==========================================================================

Provenance
----------

This repository forked the JAB Code reference implementation
(https://github.com/jabcode/jabcode) at commit ee0e4c8 on 2022-06-17, when
upstream was licensed LGPL-2.1, and carried that LGPL-2.1 text until now.

Fraunhofer SIT, the sole copyright holder of the inherited code, relicensed
the project to the MIT License in commit
3b56eef72436c88fc8538dc4d63920e058537874 on 2026-04-17.

Between the fork point and that relicense, upstream changed NOTHING under
src/ -- all three intervening upstream commits touch only LICENSE, and

    git diff ee0e4c8 upstream/master -- src/

returns empty. The code this fork inherited is therefore the identical work
that Fraunhofer now offers under the MIT License. The LGPL-2.1 text this file
previously contained was a stale copy of a superseded offer, not a separate
surviving obligation.

Every addition made in this fork since ee0e4c8 is the work of Kendall Fleming
and is offered here under the same MIT terms. Fraunhofer's copyright notice is
retained above because MIT requires it, not as a formality: the codec core
remains substantially their work.

What this file does NOT cover
-----------------------------

The jabauth-android/ subtree is PROPRIETARY and is expressly excluded from the
grant above. See jabauth-android/LICENSE.

The MIT grant in this file covers the codec and its wrappers:
src/, panama-wrapper/, swift-java-wrapper/, conformance/, and the supporting
benchmark and robustness corpora.

Third-party tooling vendored under panama-wrapper/tools/ carries its own
licence (async-profiler, Apache-2.0) and is unaffected by either grant.
